### Basis and residual patterns

@tbl-basis assesses whether the chosen basis dimensions can represent the fitted patterns. @fig-residual-patterns checks the remaining structure by time and group.


::: {#tbl-basis .cell tbl-cap='Basis checks. NA indicates that this diagnostic is unavailable for the factor term.'}

```{.r .cell-code}
basis <- bind_rows(lapply(c("clock", "phase"), function(axis) {
  table_data(paste0("primary_", axis, "_basis"), "results/diagnostics") |>
    mutate(axis = axis, .before = 1)
}))
show_table(basis)
```

