Diagnostic views for the MEQ clock-time and circadian-phase models. Each fit uses 68 participants, 379 participant-days, and 17,558 valid half-hours.
:::


The in-sample fits are very similar under both classifications and both time coordinates (@tbl-meq-fit). These values include participant and day effects. They do not establish which questionnaire or time coordinate predicts new observations better. Predictive validation and Shapley attribution remain focused on the primary near-eye sample.


::: {#tbl-meq-fit .cell tbl-cap='In-sample fit for the MEQ sensitivity and the paired MSFsc comparison. Adjusted R² is the `mgcv` estimate; ordinary R² compares residual variation with the observed response variation.'}

