## Sleep-diary midsleep and MSFsc {#sec-sleep-diary}

This separate analysis compares questionnaire-derived MSFsc with the timing of recorded sleep episodes. The main comparison includes all available diary nights from the 140 participants in the primary near-eye exposure analysis, including nights whose waking day has no retained light observations. A second comparison uses every participant with valid diary and MSFsc data in the imported cohort. The exposure models are unchanged.

### Sleep episodes and waking-day labels

Midsleep is the midpoint between diary-derived **sleep onset** and **final awakening**, using dated local-clock timestamps. Sleep onset incorporates the reported delay between trying to sleep and falling asleep; it is not bedtime. The midpoint describes the sleep period and does not redistribute time around intervening awakenings. The diary question “Today is...” supplies the work/free label for the **waking date**. Thus Saturday-to-Sunday sleep is labelled free when Sunday is free, while Sunday-to-Monday sleep is labelled work when Monday is a work day.

The code below reads the fixed input snapshot and the participant list from the primary analysis. The staged code is also available as a [standalone R script](R/sleep_diary_alignment.R).


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true" code-summary="Register the executable diary-analysis stages"}
knitr::read_chunk("R/sleep_diary_alignment.R")
```
:::



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true" code-summary="Read the diary, chronotype and primary-sample inputs"}
source(".Rprofile")
suppressPackageStartupMessages({
  library(dplyr)
  library(tidyr)
  library(ggplot2)
})
sleep_diary_manifest <- read.csv("input-data/manifest.csv") |>
  filter(role %in% c("sleepdiaries", "chronotype"))
stopifnot(identical(
  unname(tools::md5sum(sleep_diary_manifest$path)),
  sleep_diary_manifest$md5
))
sleep_diary_raw <- readRDS(
  "input-data/model_data/normalized_inputs/sleepdiaries.rds"
)
sleep_diary_chronotype <- readRDS(
  "input-data/model_data/normalized_inputs/chronotype.rds"
) |>
  transmute(site, Id, msfsc_hours = as.numeric(msf_sc) / 3600)
sleep_diary_primary <- readRDS("results/data/prepared.rds")$frames$glasses |>
  distinct(site, Id, local_date)
stopifnot(!anyDuplicated(sleep_diary_chronotype[c("site", "Id")]))
```
:::


We retain records with a valid sleep onset, awakening, MSFsc and waking-day label, respecting the upstream interval checks. Midnight is handled through the dated timestamps before extracting the midpoint's clock time. For correlation and variability, both clock variables use a fixed noon-to-noon scale, so times immediately before and after midnight remain adjacent.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
sleep_diary_records <- sleep_diary_raw |>
  left_join(
    sleep_diary_chronotype,
    by = c("site", "Id"),
    relationship = "many-to-one"
  ) |>
  left_join(
    sleep_diary_primary |>
      distinct(site, Id) |>
      mutate(in_primary_sample = TRUE),
    by = c("site", "Id"),
    relationship = "many-to-one"
  ) |>
  mutate(
    participant = paste(site, Id, sep = "::"),
    in_primary_sample = coalesce(in_primary_sample, FALSE),
    waking_date = as.Date(wake_wall, tz = "UTC"),
    daytype = factor(
      as.character(daytype2),
      levels = c("a work day", "a free day"),
      labels = c("Work", "Free")
    ),
    sleep_period_hours = as.numeric(difftime(
      wake_wall,
      sleep_onset_wall,
      units = "hours"
    )),
    midpoint_wall = sleep_onset_wall + sleep_period_hours * 3600 / 2,
    midsleep_hours = (as.numeric(midpoint_wall) / 3600) %% 24,
    # A fixed noon cut keeps times either side of midnight adjacent.
    midsleep_unwrapped_hours = ((midsleep_hours + 12) %% 24) - 12,
    msfsc_unwrapped_hours = ((msfsc_hours + 12) %% 24) - 12,
    difference_minutes = (((midsleep_hours - msfsc_hours + 12) %% 24) - 12) *
      60,
    dst_crossing = sleep_onset_utc_offset_minutes != wake_utc_offset_minutes,
    exclusion = case_when(
      !is.finite(msfsc_hours) ~ "Missing MSFsc",
      is.na(sleep_onset_wall) | is.na(wake_wall) ~
        "Missing sleep onset or awakening",
      !sleep_interval_analysis_eligible | sleep_interval_quarantined ~
        "Upstream interval quarantine",
      sleep_period_hours <= 0 | sleep_period_hours >= 24 ~
        "Invalid sleep-period duration",
      is.na(daytype) ~ "Missing waking-day type",
      TRUE ~ "Included"
    )
  ) |>
  left_join(
    sleep_diary_primary |>
      rename(waking_date = local_date) |>
      mutate(waking_date_in_light_analysis = TRUE),
    by = c("site", "Id", "waking_date"),
    relationship = "many-to-one"
  ) |>
  mutate(
    waking_date_in_light_analysis = coalesce(
      waking_date_in_light_analysis,
      FALSE
    )
  )
sleep_diary_valid <- sleep_diary_records |> filter(exclusion == "Included")
sleep_diary_nights <- sleep_diary_valid |> filter(in_primary_sample)
sleep_diary_flow <- bind_rows(
  sleep_diary_records |>
    summarise(
      stage = "All imported diary entries",
      participants = n_distinct(participant),
      nights = n()
    ),
  sleep_diary_records |>
    filter(in_primary_sample) |>
    summarise(
      stage = "Entries from primary exposure participants",
      participants = n_distinct(participant),
      nights = n()
    ),
  sleep_diary_nights |>
    summarise(
      stage = "Valid primary-sample diary nights",
      participants = n_distinct(participant),
      nights = n()
    ),
  sleep_diary_nights |>
    filter(waking_date_in_light_analysis) |>
    summarise(
      stage = "Also have waking-day light observations",
      participants = n_distinct(participant),
      nights = n()
    ),
  sleep_diary_valid |>
    summarise(
      stage = "Valid nights in all available participants",
      participants = n_distinct(participant),
      nights = n()
    )
)
sleep_diary_flow
```
