:::


The 140 primary-analysis participants supplied **972 diary entries**, of which **971** had the required timing and day-type information. One entry lacked the required sleep timing and day type. Of the retained nights, **778** correspond to waking dates in the exposure analysis and **193** provide additional diary information. There are **620 work-day nights from 139 participants** and **351 free-day nights from 136 participants**. In the full imported cohort, **1,268 valid nights from 183 participants** are available for comparison.

### Association with MSFsc

We calculate Pearson correlations between nightly midsleep and MSFsc overall and separately for work and free days. The nightly correlation weights each recorded night equally. Its 95% interval comes from 2,000 bootstrap samples of participants, carrying each selected participant's nights together. We also correlate each participant's mean diary midsleep with MSFsc, giving each participant one observation within the relevant day-type context. This second summary distinguishes habitual timing agreement from night-to-night variation; MSFsc itself does not vary across a participant's nights.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true" code-summary="Calculate correlations and resample whole participants"}
# Resample whole people, carrying all their nights together.
sleep_diary_correlations <- function(nights, context, scope, draws = 2000L) {
  selected <- if (context == "Overall") nights else
    filter(nights, daytype == context)
  people <- selected |>
    summarise(
      msfsc = first(msfsc_unwrapped_hours),
      midsleep = mean(midsleep_unwrapped_hours),
      .by = participant
    )
  stopifnot(nrow(people) >= 3L, stats::sd(people$msfsc) > 0)
  night_indices <- split(seq_len(nrow(selected)), selected$participant)
  boot <- replicate(draws, {
    chosen <- sample.int(nrow(people), nrow(people), replace = TRUE)
    ids <- people$participant[chosen]
    rows <- unlist(night_indices[ids], use.names = FALSE)
    c(
      night = stats::cor(
        selected$msfsc_unwrapped_hours[rows],
        selected$midsleep_unwrapped_hours[rows]
      ),
      participant_mean = stats::cor(
        people$msfsc[chosen],
        people$midsleep[chosen]
      )
    )
  })
  stopifnot(all(is.finite(boot)))
  tibble::tibble(
    scope = scope,
    context = context,
    participants = nrow(people),
    nights = nrow(selected),
    night_r = stats::cor(
      selected$msfsc_unwrapped_hours,
      selected$midsleep_unwrapped_hours
    ),
    night_lower = unname(stats::quantile(boot["night", ], 0.025)),
    night_upper = unname(stats::quantile(boot["night", ], 0.975)),
    participant_mean_r = stats::cor(people$msfsc, people$midsleep),
    participant_mean_lower = unname(stats::quantile(
      boot["participant_mean", ],
      0.025
    )),
    participant_mean_upper = unname(stats::quantile(
      boot["participant_mean", ],
      0.975
    )),
    median_difference_minutes = stats::median(selected$difference_minutes),
    median_absolute_difference_minutes = stats::median(abs(
      selected$difference_minutes
    )),
    bootstrap_draws = draws
  )
}
```
