Across **139 participants with at least three nights**, the median within-participant SD was **47 minutes (interquartile range 34–62 minutes)**. Within day types, the median was **30 minutes on work days** and **35 minutes on free days**, based on **127** and **59** eligible participants, respectively. The stronger association after averaging nights and the remaining nightly variation show that MSFsc tracks habitual sleep timing but does not locate each night's actual midpoint.

### Diary-derived MSFsc equivalent (MSF~sc(diary)~)

We also construct a diary-derived MSFsc equivalent (MSF~sc(diary)~) from the recorded sleep episodes. For each participant, we average midsleep and sleep-period duration separately before work days and free days. The correction follows the [MCTQ sleep-debt formula](https://docs.ropensci.org/mctq/reference/msf_sc.html), replacing the usual weekly work/free-day weights with the **observed numbers of valid diary nights** in each category. With mean durations $SD_W$ and $SD_F$ and counts $n_W$ and $n_F$,

$$
\overline{SD}_{\mathrm{diary}} =
\frac{n_W SD_W+n_F SD_F}{n_W+n_F},
\qquad
\mathrm{MSF}_{\mathrm{sc(diary)}} = MSF_{\mathrm{diary}}
-\frac{\max(0,SD_F-\overline{SD}_{\mathrm{diary}})}{2}.
$$

Thus work-day sleep duration and the recorded day counts determine the correction to mean free-day midsleep. Work-day and free-day midsleep are not themselves averaged to obtain the corrected value. If free-day sleep is no longer than work-day sleep, the correction is zero. Durations use the same local-clock interval from sleep onset to final awakening as the midsleep calculation. Each participant needs at least one valid night of both types. The diaries have no alarm-use field, so this is a diary-derived equivalent rather than a full MCTQ re-scoring.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
sleep_diary_daytype_means <- sleep_diary_nights |>
  summarise(
    nights = n(),
    midsleep = mean(midsleep_unwrapped_hours),
    sleep_duration = mean(sleep_period_hours),
    .by = c(site, Id, participant, msfsc_unwrapped_hours, daytype)
  )
sleep_diary_msfsc_participants <- sleep_diary_daytype_means |>
  pivot_wider(
    names_from = daytype,
    values_from = c(nights, midsleep, sleep_duration),
    values_fill = list(nights = 0L)
  ) |>
  rename(
    work_nights = nights_Work,
    free_nights = nights_Free,
    msw_hours = midsleep_Work,
    msf_hours = midsleep_Free,
    sd_work_hours = sleep_duration_Work,
    sd_free_hours = sleep_duration_Free
  ) |>
  mutate(
    eligible = work_nights > 0L & free_nights > 0L,
    mean_sleep_duration_hours = if_else(
      eligible,
      (work_nights * sd_work_hours + free_nights * sd_free_hours) /
        (work_nights + free_nights),
      NA_real_
    ),
    correction_hours = if_else(
      eligible,
      pmax(0, sd_free_hours - mean_sleep_duration_hours) / 2,
      NA_real_
    ),
    diary_msfsc_hours = msf_hours - correction_hours,
    difference_minutes = (diary_msfsc_hours - msfsc_unwrapped_hours) * 60
  )
sleep_diary_msfsc_eligible <- sleep_diary_msfsc_participants |>
  filter(eligible)
sleep_diary_msfsc_flow <- sleep_diary_msfsc_participants |>
  summarise(
    primary_participants = n(),
    eligible_participants = sum(eligible),
    missing_work_nights = sum(work_nights == 0L),
    missing_free_nights = sum(free_nights == 0L),
    work_nights = sum(work_nights[eligible]),
    free_nights = sum(free_nights[eligible]),
    corrected_participants = sum(correction_hours > 0, na.rm = TRUE),
    median_correction_minutes = stats::median(correction_hours, na.rm = TRUE) *
      60
  )
sleep_diary_msfsc_flow
```

